cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Paper Reproduction Template
message: >-
  If you use this template, please cite the paper it accompanies
  (see preferred-citation below).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dominik
    family-names: Köster
    email: dominik.koester@oth-regensburg.de
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0230-3123'
    affiliation: >-
      Technical University of Applied Sciences Regensburg (OTH Regensburg)
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/paper-reproduction-template'
abstract: >-
  A self-contained project template for reproducible papers: a Makefile-driven
  pipeline from experiment scripts through generated data and figures to a
  camera-ready IEEEtran PDF, with three levels of environment pinning
  (requirements.txt, Docker, Nix) and a reference-result check.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - reproduction package
  - research software
  - quantum computing
  - LaTeX

# The template is a contribution of the paper below; cite the paper rather
# than the repository.
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: 'Works on My QPU: Reproducibility in Quantum Computing Research'
